.TITLE "free"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Displays the amount of free and used physical and swap memory in the system. It provides a quick __overview of RAM__ consumption and available resources.

.DIV "TLDR"
**free**
Displays memory usage in kilobytes by default.
> 

**free -h**
Displays memory usage in human-readable formats like GB or MB.
> __-h__ human-readable flag

**free -s number**
Continuously displays memory usage every few seconds.
> __-s__ seconds flag | __number__ the interval duration

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __free -h__ is the standard way to check if your system is running low on RAM. Note that the "available" column is usually a better indicator of free memory than the "free" column, as it includes memory currently used for caching that can be reclaimed.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**cli:top** **cli:vmstat** **cli:lsblk**

documentation: __https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man1/free.1.html__
